## Task 1 — UK Road Safety Data: Summary Output (Power BI)

| Dashboard Visual | Output / Result |
|---|---|
| Geographical distribution map | Highest accident density in London, Manchester, and Birmingham |
| Monthly trend line chart | Accident counts fluctuate seasonally, peaking around holiday periods |
| Weather condition pie chart | Majority of accidents occur in clear weather, not adverse conditions |
| Severity bar chart | Slight accidents far outnumber serious and fatal accidents |
| Time-of-day chart | Afternoon hours show the highest collision frequency |
| Speed limit chart | Lower speed-limit zones show a higher accident count than expected |
| Road type treemap | Single carriageway roads account for the largest share of accidents |

**Overall Result:** Urban, clear-weather, afternoon conditions on single carriageway roads represent the highest-risk combination for UK road accidents — pointing toward targeted safety interventions in cities and infrastructure reviews for single carriageway design.
